# Test specimens are byte-exact fixtures: each one's SHA-256 is recorded in
# the registry and checked before the test that reads it, so that a file which
# has been altered is caught rather than quietly producing a different
# reading. Git must therefore never rewrite them.
#
# Several vendor formats are text-shaped — Nanonis .dat is ASCII throughout,
# WSxM .top has a text header — so git's own heuristic treats them as text and
# a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf converts every LF to CRLF. That
# changes the bytes and the checksum no longer matches the file the reference
# was captured from. Marking the directory binary pins the bytes on every
# platform, and covers formats added later without anyone having to remember.
gwyddionpy/tests/data/** binary

# The captured references and notes beside the specimens are reviewed as text,
# so keep them diffable — pinned to LF so they are identical everywhere.
gwyddionpy/tests/data/**/*.json text eol=lf diff
gwyddionpy/tests/data/README.md text eol=lf diff
